    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div style=\"color:#000;background-color:#fff;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><div style=\"display:block\"><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><div style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue,Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Para:</span></b> Cristiano Trinca &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">cttr...@yahoo.com.br</a>&gt; <br><b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Cc:</span></b> secr &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">secr...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br> <b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Enviadas:</span></b> Quinta-feira, 25 de Maio de 2017 21:29</font></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div style=\"color:#000;background-color:#fff;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><div style=\"display:block\"><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><div style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue,Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><br> <b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Assunto:</span></b> Re: detection probability of each individual<br> </font></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div style=\"color:#000;background-color:#fff;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><div style=\"display:block\"><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><div style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue,Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><div><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Yes, but (i) you don&#39;t know the location of each individual and (ii) you will otherwise get the same result for every animal. You need to think through what you really want and why, then ask a better question.<br clear=\"none\"></div>Murray<br clear=\"none\"><div><br clear=\"none\"></div></div><div><div><br clear=\"none\"><div>On Fri, May 26, 2017 at 12:19 PM, &#39;Cristiano Trinca&#39; via secr <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\" shape=\"rect\" href data-email-masked>secr...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br clear=\"none\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div style=\"color:#000;background-color:#fff;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><div><span>HiEfford, thanks for your answer.</span></div><div><span><br clear=\"none\"></span></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><span>So, it is correct to use pdot with the coordinates of the centers of activity to estimate the detection probabilities for each individual separately?</span></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><span><br clear=\"none\"></span></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><span>Cristiano</span></div><div><br clear=\"none\"><br clear=\"none\"></div><div style=\"display:block\">  <div style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"> <div style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue,Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"> <div dir=\"ltr\"> <font size=\"2\" face=\"Arial\"><span> </span></font><hr size=\"1\"> <b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">De:</span></b> Murray Efford &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\" shape=\"rect\" href data-email-masked>murray...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br clear=\"none\"> <b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Para:</span></b> secr &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\" shape=\"rect\" href data-email-masked>secr...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; <br clear=\"none\"><b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Cc:</span></b> <a rel=\"nofollow\" shape=\"rect\" href data-email-masked>cttr...@yahoo.com.br</a><br clear=\"none\"> <b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Enviadas:</span></b> Quinta-feira, 25 de Maio de 2017 17:24<span><br clear=\"none\"> <b><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Assunto:</span></b> Re: detection probability of each individual<br clear=\"none\"> </span> </div><div><div> <div><br clear=\"none\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><span>...if each individual have different capture histories,\r\n so they will have different detection probabilities...</span><br clear=\"none\"></blockquote><br clear=\"none\"></blockquote><div> This does not follow. Capture histories result from a stochastic sampling process: they will differ even for animals at the same location with the same detection probability.<br clear=\"none\"><br clear=\"none\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"> I don&#39;t think that this estimate represent the \r\nprobability of that individual to be detect by the trap grid. <br clear=\"none\"></blockquote><div><br clear=\"none\">I disagree.<br clear=\"none\"> <br clear=\"none\"></div></div>On Thursday, May 25, 2017 at 12:11:50 AM UTC+12, cttrinca wrote:<blockquote style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><div style=\"color:#000;background-color:#fff;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Group,<br clear=\"none\"></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br clear=\"none\"></div><div dir=\"ltr\">does anyone know how to estimate the detection probability of each individual?</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br clear=\"none\"></div><div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks,</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br clear=\"none\"></div><div dir=\"ltr\">Cristiano<br clear=\"none\"></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div>\r\n\r\n<div></div>\r\n\r\n-- <br clear=\"none\">\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;secr&quot; group.<br clear=\"none\">\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\" shape=\"rect\" href data-email-masked>secrgroup+unsubscribe@ googlegroups.com</a>.<br clear=\"none\">\r\nFor more options, visit <a rel=\"nofollow\" shape=\"rect\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487925204000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2QIhf4XofdQ7YjKoKy2HeC\">https://groups.google.com/d/ optout</a>.<br clear=\"none\"></div></div><br clear=\"none\"><br clear=\"none\"></div> </div></div></div> </div>  </div></div></div><div><div>\r\n\r\n<div></div>\r\n\r\n-- <br clear=\"none\">\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;secr&quot; group.<br clear=\"none\">\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\" shape=\"rect\" href data-email-masked>secrgroup+unsubscribe@ googlegroups.com</a>.<br clear=\"none\">\r\nFor more options, visit <a rel=\"nofollow\" shape=\"rect\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487925204000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2QIhf4XofdQ7YjKoKy2HeC\">https://groups.google.com/d/ optout</a>.<br clear